      "isAutoRefreshDisabled": false,
      "markdown": "## Public Endpoint Traffic & CloudFront Caching\nThe public status list and JWKS are served by CloudFront from S3 (they never hit API Gateway). Replace `CLOUDFRONT_DISTRIBUTION_ID` with the real distribution id. **Note:** CloudFront CloudWatch metrics are per-distribution and cannot be split by path/behaviour, so status-list vs JWKS traffic cannot be separated from standard metrics — use CloudFront access logs (already enabled) for a per-path breakdown."
    },
    {
      "name": "Markdown",
      "tileType": "MARKDOWN",
      "configured": true,
      "bounds": {
        "top": 760,
        "left": 0,
        "width": 2280,
        "height": 38
      },
      "tileFilter": {},
      "isAutoRefreshDisabled": false,
      "markdown": "## List Lifecycle\nRenewals, publishing and fill levels. These use the `CrsBackend` EMF namespace emitted by the Lambdas. `StatusListPercentageFill` has **no list-id dimension** today (flagged in the ticket), so it is an aggregate only. “Published lists by signing key” has no metric — the `kid` lives only in logs / S3 object metadata (see placeholder tile)."
    },
    {
      "name": "Markdown",
      "tileType": "MARKDOWN",
      "configured": true,
      "bounds": {
        "top": 1064,
        "left": 0,
        "width": 2280,
        "height": 38
      },
      "tileFilter": {},
      "isAutoRefreshDisabled": false,
      "markdown": "## End-to-End Timing\nTime taken from the API Gateway request to completion, using API Gateway `Latency` (includes Lambda execution). A true end-to-end business duration EMF metric (`IssuedStatusDuration`) is defined in code but not currently emitted — API Gateway latency is the closest available proxy."
    },
